{{!< default}}
{{!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     post — THE DISPATCHER.
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------
     Ghost gives a theme exactly one post.hbs for every post on the site, and
     this theme has kinds of post that are genuinely different PAGES — a
     course is an overview with a curriculum, a lesson is a reading surface
     with a way back, a blog post is an article. So this file renders nothing
     itself. It reads tags and hands off.

     ⚠ BRANCH ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING. The PARENT of each pair is tested before
     its child — #course before #lesson, #docs-section before #docs-page —
     because an overview is not a lesson, and matching the lesson branch would
     render a course overview inside a lesson layout. A new branch goes where
     its SPECIFICITY demands, not at the end: ask whether any post carries
     both this tag and one already in the list, and if so put the more
     specific one first.

     default.hbs forks on the SAME tags to swap the chrome, so a reading
     surface does not get a marketing bar. THE TWO LISTS MUST STAY IN
     AGREEMENT — if a kind moves from marketing chrome to reading chrome it
     changes in both files, or the page gets a bar that contradicts its body.

     The fallback is not optional. A post carrying none of these tags still
     has to render, and it gets the same surface a blog post gets, because an
     untyped post is still a post.
     ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ --}}

{{#post}}
    {{#has tag="#course"}}
        {{> "post/parent" kind=(t "Course") childWord=(t "lesson") childWordPlural=(t "lessons") childKind="lesson"}}
    {{else has tag="#training-module"}}
        {{> "post/training-section"}}
    {{else has tag="#docs-section"}}
        {{> "post/parent" kind=(t "Section") childWord=(t "page") childWordPlural=(t "pages") childKind="unit"}}
    {{else has tag="#lesson, #training-lesson, #docs-page"}}
        {{> "post/lesson"}}
    {{else}}
        {{> "post/default"}}
    {{/has}}
{{/post}}
